2026-11-05T23:55:57.1634295Z             "body": "The [Community post-merge run](https://github.com/princessdardan/lash-her-community-api/actions/runs/42130005740) at `a454702be10362a4054f60579e92aa3b4641ff51` refused native qualification while rebuilding the independent zlib reference. The captured stderr contains the expected unpatched assertion, but the Python subprocess return code was omitted, so the failed `returncode == -6` condition cannot yet be explained.\n\nThis adds one structured diagnostic before the existing assertion: direct-child return code and signal number, expected SIGABRT value, assertion-text presence, Python/platform/kernel and core limit. If the reproducer returns an unexpected code, a separate Python SIGABRT control records signal reporting in the same build environment. The exact `-6` plus expected-stderr acceptance predicate remains unchanged; no exit status is normalized or newly accepted. Only `build.sh` and its self-pinned implementation hash change.\n\nOn POSIX, [Python reports signal termination as a negative signal number](https://docs.python.org/3/library/subprocess.html#subprocess.CompletedProcess.returncode). Thus `-6` is SIGABRT; a positive code such as 134 would remain a process exit code in this direct, shell-free invocation and would still fail. The actual unexpected code in the original run is unknown.\n\nBefore this diagnostic, the native builder/input lock, source/package descriptor, upstream/backport patches, build script, reproducer and verifier were byte-identical to passed Course main `61c7024e`; only the service-specific runtime README differed. Source inputs, patches, package version, installed-image checks and HIGH/CRITICAL enforcement remain unchanged.\n\nValidation on `fe9015bacfa839499a1b705dbcc69921c8bb7b30`:\n\n- `npm run verify`: 364 tests plus TypeScript, lint, contracts, migrations/schema drift and OpenAPI checks passed.\n- Native qualification guards: 26 passed.\n- Five simulated diagnostic cases preserve the existing predicate: expected SIGABRT/assertion passes; zero, SIGSEGV, positive 134 and wrong assertion refuse.\n- Shell syntax check passed. OpenAPI and enrollment schema bytes are unchanged.\n\nLocal Linux image reproduction is unavailable because the Docker daemon socket is absent. This draft prepares an instrumented CI run; it does not qualify the existing failed main artifact, change the native acceptance policy, authorize deployment, or alter frontend PR 91.",
