2026-11-05T23:58:48.5443157Z [36;1m[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5443846Z [36;1m# The following logic implements the configuration priority described in the README:[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5444663Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5445041Z [36;1m# Inputs[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5445467Z [36;1m# Environment Variables[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5445968Z [36;1m# Config File[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5446418Z [36;1m# Defaults[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5446822Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5447602Z [36;1m# As noted above defaults are awkward to handle as GitHub Actions will inject those values as the input[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5448852Z [36;1m# if the caller doesn't provide them, thus if the input matches the default we don't set it as we[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5449769Z [36;1m# can't tell the difference.  Plus if we did set it when it was the default value then it could potentially[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5451453Z [36;1m# override an external environment variable, or something in the callers configuration file, which then wouldn't[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5452290Z [36;1m# match the configuration priority that is documented.[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5453125Z [36;1mset_env_var_if_provided() {[0m
2026-11-05T23:58:48.5453650Z [36;1m  local var_name="$1"[0m
